<title>CHINA: SHANGHAI RESIDENTS PREFER TO BUY &quot;MADE IN CHINA&quot;.</title>
<headline>SHANGHAI RESIDENTS PREFER TO BUY &quot;MADE IN CHINA&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai residents prefer buying domestically-produced goods, especially top-brand commodities, rather than imports, the Xinmin Evening News said on Monday.</p>
<p>A survey of newlyweds in the city found that 80 percent of the goods they bought to set up their new homes were domestically produced, up from 60 percent a year ago, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>It had no further details.</p>
<p>-- Shanghai Newsroom (8621) 6279-7004 Fax: 6279-7174</p>
